note The io-store crate: the one place the program writes or removes a file (clippy's disallowed-methods sends every other crate here). A write goes to a temporary file beside the target and is renamed over it, so a reader never sees half a file: the map store, the index cache and screenshots all save through it. On Windows a file another process holds open (an editor, a virus scanner, the indexer) refuses the write or rename for a moment; those error codes are retried a few times with a short pause, anything else fails at once.

